"""Patient-facing copy and primary references. No invented clinical reviewer or services."""

CDCP_BODY = '''
<h2>Before your appointment</h2>
<p>Bring your CDCP member information or private insurance details, along with photo ID. For CDCP, check that your coverage has started and is still active. Tell the office when booking that you plan to use it.</p>
<h2>Will I have anything to pay?</h2>
<p>CDCP does not necessarily pay the whole bill. Your share can include a co-payment, fees above the plan's reimbursement amount, or services the plan does not cover. Some treatment needs approval in advance. Ask for an estimate before agreeing to treatment.</p>
<p>Private plans also have their own limits and exclusions. Direct billing does not mean every charge is covered. Bring your plan details so the office can help you check.</p>
<h2>Eligibility and applications</h2>
<p>The Government of Canada decides CDCP eligibility. Check its current requirements and application process rather than relying on a website calculator. The clinic cannot confirm eligibility from your income alone.</p>
<p><a href="https://www.canada.ca/en/services/benefits/dental/dental-care-plan/qualify.html">Check official CDCP eligibility requirements</a> · <a href="https://www.canada.ca/en/services/benefits/dental/dental-care-plan/apply.html">Apply or renew through Canada.ca</a></p>
<h2>Questions to ask before treatment</h2>
<ul class="list"><li>What treatment is recommended, and what are my alternatives?</li><li>What is the total estimate and my expected share?</li><li>Does anything need preauthorization?</li><li>Could the estimate change, and when would we discuss that?</li></ul>
<p>For the program rules, see <a href="https://www.canada.ca/en/services/benefits/dental/dental-care-plan/coverage.html">Health Canada's coverage information</a> and <a href="https://www.canada.ca/en/services/benefits/dental/dental-care-plan/guide.html">Dental Benefits Guide</a>.</p>
'''
CDCP_FAQS = [
    ('Does 109 Dental accept CDCP?', 'Yes. 109 Dental accepts the Canadian Dental Care Plan. Tell the office when booking and bring your member details so coverage can be checked.'),
    ('Does CDCP mean my visit is free?', 'Not necessarily. You may have a co-payment, a difference between the clinic fee and the plan reimbursement, or charges for treatment that is not covered. Ask for an estimate before treatment.'),
    ('Can I use CDCP before my coverage starts?', 'Check your coverage start date before booking treatment under the plan. An application or approval notice alone does not mean coverage has already started.'),
    ('Does CDCP cover implants?', 'CDCP does not cover dental implants or implant-related procedures. Ask about the cost and any private benefits before choosing treatment.'),
]

SERVICE_ADDITIONS = {
    'wisdom-teeth': '''<h2>Questions for your assessment</h2><p>You do not need to decide on removal before you call. Ask whether existing x-rays can be transferred, who would carry out the procedure, and whether referral is appropriate. Discuss the anaesthetic or sedation options available for your case before booking treatment.</p><h2>Cost, time off, and getting home</h2><p>Ask for an estimate that explains what is included. Before choosing a treatment date, ask about time away from work or classes, follow-up visits, and whether you need someone to take you home. These details depend on the planned procedure.</p><p>For background on assessment and monitoring, see the <a href="https://www.mouthhealthy.org/all-topics-a-z/wisdom-teeth">American Dental Association's wisdom-teeth information</a>.</p>''',
    'family-dentistry': '''<h2>Your first visit</h2><p>Bring a medication list, insurance or CDCP details, and any recent dental records. Tell us about pain, sensitivity, previous treatment, or anything that makes dental visits difficult. Call ahead if you want to arrange record transfer.</p><h2>Checkups, cleaning, and fillings</h2><p>A checkup and a cleaning serve different purposes. An exam helps identify concerns; a hygiene appointment addresses plaque and tartar. Ask what is included in the appointment you book. If a filling or other treatment is recommended, ask about the options and estimate before deciding.</p><h2>Planning ongoing care</h2><p>Appointment frequency should fit your needs. Ask your dentist when to return and what to focus on at home. If several family members need visits, call to discuss available times.</p>''',
    'emergency-dentist': '''<h2>What to tell us when you call</h2><p>Describe what happened, when symptoms began, and whether there is swelling, bleeding, an injury, or a broken tooth. Tell us whether you are already a patient. Calling is the quickest way to ask about availability; the appointment form is not monitored for urgent care.</p><h2>Assessment comes first</h2><p>Ask what can be assessed at the initial visit, whether further treatment may need a separate appointment, and what the estimated charges are. Same-day availability is not guaranteed.</p><p>For general first-aid information, see the <a href="https://www.mouthhealthy.org/all-topics-a-z/dental-emergencies">American Dental Association's emergency guidance</a>. For a life-threatening emergency, call 911.</p><p><a href="/how-to-handle-dental-emergencies-in-the-family/">Planning for a family dental emergency</a></p>''',
    'orthodontics-invisalign': '''<h2>What to ask at a consultation</h2><p>Bring any previous orthodontic records. Ask whether aligners are suitable for your teeth and bite, whether another approach or a referral would be appropriate, and which dentist would oversee your care.</p><h2>Understand the full plan</h2><p>Before starting, ask about the total estimate, appointment schedule, what happens if an aligner is lost, and whether retainers and follow-up are included. Treatment length and daily wear instructions depend on your individual plan.</p><p><a href="/how-do-i-care-for-my-invisalign-aligners/">Looking after your aligners</a> · <a href="https://www.mouthhealthy.org/all-topics-a-z/braces">ADA information about orthodontic options</a></p>''',
    'dental-implants': '''<h2>Before deciding on an implant</h2><p>Ask about the assessment, alternatives, stages of treatment, and who would provide each stage. Request an estimate that distinguishes the implant, replacement tooth, and any additional procedures.</p><p><a href="/can-i-get-dental-implants-if-i-have-bone-loss/">Questions about implants and bone loss</a> · <a href="/services/bone-augmentation-and-grafting/">Bone grafting questions</a> · <a href="/services/dentures/">Dentures and replacement options</a></p>''',
    'crowns-bridges': '''<h2>Before treatment</h2><p>Ask how the proposed restoration would be supported, what happens to the neighbouring teeth, how it is cleaned, and what follow-up is needed. Bring insurance details and request an estimate before treatment.</p><p><a href="/pros-and-cons-of-dental-bridges-is-this-the-right-solution-for-your-missing-teeth/">Questions to ask when comparing a bridge with other options</a></p>''',
    'cosmetic-dentistry': '''<h2>Whitening, veneers, and bonding</h2><p>Ask which option addresses your concern, whether any tooth preparation is needed, and what maintenance or replacement could involve. Discuss the likely result and limitations before deciding. A photograph alone cannot establish which treatment is suitable.</p><h2>Gum shape and your smile</h2><p>If you are asking about a gum lift or laser gum contouring, start by discussing your gum health and the result you want. Ask whether the procedure is available for your case and whether a referral is needed. A particular technique is not suitable for everyone.</p>''',
    'childrens-dentistry': '''<h2>Help us prepare for your child's visit</h2><p>Tell the office your child's age, the reason for the appointment, and any previous difficult experiences. Ask what to bring and whether there is anything to discuss before the visit.</p><p><a href="/services/jaw-development-therapy/">Questions about growth, crowding, and orthodontic assessment</a> · <a href="/services/frenulopasty-and-frenectomy/">Tongue-tie and frenectomy questions</a></p>''',
}

