 'Pain, locking, or difficulty moving your jaw deserves an assessment. A treatment name alone does not establish the cause.',
 '''<h2>TMJ and TMD</h2><p>TMJ refers to the jaw joint. TMD refers to disorders involving the jaw joints or chewing muscles. Similar symptoms can have different causes.</p><h2>Describe the pattern</h2><p>Tell the dentist when symptoms began, what makes them worse, whether your jaw locks, and what treatment you have already tried. Bring any previous reports or appliances.</p><h2>Discuss options before changing your bite</h2><p>Ask about the evidence, risks, and alternatives before agreeing to treatment that permanently changes teeth or the bite. If you have been advised to consider neuromuscular treatment or disclusion time reduction, ask what the diagnosis is and why that approach is being recommended. NIDCR advises caution about treatments that make permanent changes for TMD.</p>''',
