 '''<h2>Sleep care is different from sedation</h2><p>This page concerns sleep-related breathing and oral appliances. If you are asking about being sedated for a dental procedure, call the office to discuss what is available for your treatment.</p><h2>Start with your medical provider</h2><p>Sleep apnea treatment depends on the diagnosis and may involve a breathing device, an oral appliance, or other care. Ask your medical provider which options fit your situation. Do not stop prescribed treatment without discussing it with them.</p><h2>Before choosing an appliance</h2><p>Bring your sleep-study results and current treatment details. Ask how the appliance would be fitted, monitored, and assessed for effectiveness. If you are asking about a named system such as Vivos, confirm availability and discuss its evidence and suitability with your treating clinicians.</p>''',
