 'A tight band of tissue does not always need treatment. Assessment should focus on the difficulties a person is experiencing.',
 '''<h2>When to ask for advice</h2><p>Tongue-tie can restrict tongue movement, but some people have no problems from it. If an infant has feeding difficulties, speak with their medical provider and a qualified feeding professional rather than relying on an online description.</p><h2>Before a procedure</h2><p>Ask what problem treatment is intended to address, whether other support or assessment is needed first, and what the benefits, risks, and alternatives are. Discuss who would perform a frenectomy or frenuloplasty and what follow-up is required.</p><h2>Booking for a child</h2><p>Tell the office the child's age and the reason for the referral. Confirm whether the assessment or procedure is available for that age and situation before arranging treatment.</p>''',
